{% block demo_examples %}
## Examples

The examples run on the bundled synthetic experiment, `load_ab_test()`, with its
assignment table, `load_ab_test_assignment()`, as `assignment`.

### A capped vocabulary for the transition screen

<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.ab_compression(
    ("exp_group", "treatment", "control"),
    assignment=assignment,
    keep=["quick_add", "cart"],
    max_events=10,
)`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/ab-compression/transitions-capped.html" height={640} />

The stream is dense (90 of 92 edges testable), so the default plan keeps it as it
is; the cap of 10 events merges `checkout_start+payment` and drops four rare
events, each of them only between events that already follow each other
directly. All 58 edges of the compressed screen are testable, at a cost the
chart shows: a quarter of the transitions dropped with those events, and a
higher median MDE.

### The step screen's plan

<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.ab_compression(
    ("exp_group", "treatment", "control"),
    "steps",
    max_steps=8,
    assignment=assignment,
    keep=["quick_add"],
    max_events=10,
)`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/ab-compression/steps-capped.html" height={640} />

The same cap on the step screen relabels the rare events `other` instead of
dropping them: the transition mass stays where it was, and every later event
keeps its step.
